        <dictScrap type="liebermann"><hi rend="bold">æðeling</hi> <hi rend="italic">königlicher Prinz</hi>. <hi rend="italic">Lateinisch zu eng <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:erklart"><abbr>erklärt</abbr></ref></hi>: filius regis de legali coniuge [<hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:vielleicht"><abbr>viell.</abbr></ref> im</hi> <hi rend="italic">Hinblick <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:auf"><abbr>auf</abbr></ref></hi> <hi rend="italic">Wilhelm</hi> Ætheling † 1120] In Cn III 56,2; filius regis <ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 58,1 <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Quadr">Q</ref>; regulus <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:ubersetzt"><abbr>übs</abbr></ref></hi>. In; basilides Cons; filius regum, <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:aber"><abbr>aber</abbr></ref> Beiname Eadgars, des Sohnessohns</hi> <hi rend="italic">Eadmunds</hi> <hi rend="italic">II</hi>, <ref type="lawCode" target="law:ECf">ECf</ref> 35,1–1d = <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Lond">Lond</ref> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:ECf">ECf</ref> 35,1 A1 (<hi rend="italic">Var</hi>. aðe~, eþe~ ede~, adþe~, ade~, adl~, eade~, eadl~); <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:erklart"><abbr>erklärt</abbr></ref> <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:aus"><abbr>aus</abbr></ref></hi> aðel <hi rend="italic">und</hi> [<hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:irrig"><abbr>irrig</abbr></ref></hi>] ling: nobilis ymago 35,1d | <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Genitiv"><abbr>gn</abbr></ref></hi>: ~ges Norðleod 2. <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Grith">Grið</ref> 11; -gces <ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 58,1 | <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Dativ"><abbr>dt</abbr></ref></hi>: -ge <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Grith">Grið</ref> 12 | <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:accusativus"><abbr>ac</abbr></ref></hi>: ~ 4. — <hi